{
  "_comment": "Invented app for the enforced privacy policies (WTF-423): the backend workflows of test/support/target/workflows/backend.json and the pages of test/support/target/phoenix/page_data.json, with privacy rules on Task and a file field. scripts/phoenix_compile_check.sh renders it with privacy: :enforced and runs test/support/target/phoenix/enforced_behavior.exs, which must pass, and renders it with privacy: :omit, where the same tests must fail. Note (WTF-457): everyone finds every note and views its Title only; its owner views everything (its Score makes the owner's field policy head 100 columns, where Elixir 1.17/1.18 and 1.19+ format it differently unless the generator breaks it, WTF-459). The index page lists the flagged notes (a search constrained on Flagged, a field only the owner views): a user finds only the flagged notes they own (stricter than Bubble, which matches the stored value for every user who may search by it). Memo (WTF-475): only admins (the Current User's Admin is yes) find and view memos; the index page lists them, so a user demoted while the page is open stops seeing them on the next read, however narrow.",
